title: Device-code phishing lure
severity: high
score: 55
tags: consent-phishing, phishing
attack: T1566.002, T1528
description: A non-Microsoft page sends the visitor to Microsoft's real device-code sign-in
  (microsoft.com/devicelogin, aka.ms/devicelogin, oauth2/deviceauth). It also shows a
  code to enter, or a shared-document pretext with an email-only form. The victim
  authorises the attacker's device on Microsoft itself, so no clone is present.
---
// A foreign page hands off to Microsoft's device-code sign-in (device_code_handoffs)
// and one of its frames shows a code or share lure (device_code_lure_frames).
device_code_handoffs
| where exists(device_code_lure_frames)
